{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdALLeEa9oWbYW81yPiwE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rework complete and committed. Summary:\n\n## What the review flagged\n`_win_quote` MSVCRT-quoted each Windows trailing data arg but left the double quotes cmd.exe acts on. A value combining a literal `\"` with `&`/`|` (e.g. `a\"&b`) ended cmd.exe's quoted region early and re-exposed the separator to the shell — violating WI-227's ruled data contract for that whole input class. I reproduced it on this Windows box (`a\"&b` → program got `a\"`; `a\"|b` → crash).\n\n## The fix (enforce the contract, not document a limit)\nAdded a **phase-2 caret pass** to `_win_quote`: after MSVCRT quoting, prefix `^` to every cmd.exe metacharacter in the result — the separators/redirects `& | < > ( ) ^` **and the `\"` chars phase 1 added**. cmd.exe then treats each `\"` as a non-toggling literal, never enters a quoted region, and passes the token through whole for the program's own argv parser to recover. Verified empirically: `a\"&b`, `a\"|b`, `a\"&b|c`, `a b\"&c` all now reach the program as one literal token.\n\n`%` is deliberately excluded from the caret set — cmd.exe expands `%VAR%`/`!VAR!` *before* caret processing, so that stays the one honest, documented residual limit.\n\n(Caught and fixed a bug in my own first draft of the phase-2 pass: it iterated the quoting *list*'s multi-char elements instead of characters, so the inner `\\\"` escaped nothing — the unit tests caught it where my standalone experiment hadn't. Fixed by joining first, then escaping per character.)\n\n## Tests\nAdded three cross-platform regressions combining `\"` with `&`, `|`, and both at once (`a\"&b`, `a\"|b`, `a\"&b|c`, `a b\"&c`) to the existing data-arg parametrization — Windows exercises the caret fix, `shlex.quote` already covered POSIX. All proven failing pre-fix.\n\n## Verification (real output)\n- `run_menu` suite: **20 passed, 1 skipped**\n- Smoke tier: **854 passed, 3 skipped**\n- Full unfiltered suite: **1084 passed, 4 skipped**\n- ruff format + lint (Python 3.8): clean\n\n## Docs\nUpdated the module docstring, `_win_quote` docstring, and `docs/specs/WI-227.md` ruling — limit (b) is now *eliminated* (not documented), with the review-remediation history recorded honestly.\n\nCommitted as `8d3f5bf` with the `WI-227` / `Train` / `Base` trailers. No coordination truth touched (only `run_menu.py`, `test_run_menu.py`, `WI-227.md` changed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":96269,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8129915d-af74-417e-9484-18e89a7f2f16","uuid":"f9c8cef7-9477-47d6-9743-ed3a67d84788","request_id":"req_011CdALLd4sQDr9XrXEUkEvV"}
